{
 "title": "Was Stalin Necessary? Counterfactual Evidence on Soviet Growth - Replication Spec",
 "hypothesis": "Observed Russian-core growth after 1928 exceeds ordinary admissible counterfactuals; does not exceed all hostile upper bounds; SUN does not exceed ASCF-90.",
 "data_sources": [
  "Global Macro Database - Russian-core GDP and GDP per capita, donor panels",
  "Maddison Project Database 2023 - alternative GDP per capita RUS and SUN",
  "CIA/RAND Soviet national accounts - GNP growth sector and end-use",
  "Markevich-Harrison appendix 1913-1928 war/civil-war/NEP bridge",
  "COW / Federico-Tena / JST / Barro-Lee trade, macro-financial, human-capital diagnostics"
 ],
 "sample": "Treated units: GMD RUS, Maddison RUS, Maddison SUN. Donor panel historical output 1900-1940 (~28 countries, LOO leaves 27). Treated treatment = realized post-1928 regime package (Five-Year Plan, collectivisation, reallocation) vs specified alternatives. No sampling weights.",
 "period_start": "1900",
 "period_end": "1940",
 "method": [
  "1. Normalize every observed and counterfactual path to 1928=100: recover y1928=y1929-g1929 (first log level minus first annual log growth), plot 100*exp(y_t - y1928). Principal endpoint 1938; sensitivities 1933,1934,1936,1940. 1939-1940 treated as mobilisation sensitivity.",
  "2. Primary causal estimators on GMD RUS and Maddison RUS/SUN: Augmented SCM with ridge bias correction; Synthetic Difference-in-Differences with unit and time weights plus bias correction; Generalized Synthetic Control via donor PCA/factor ridge interactive fixed effects; Matrix Completion via low-rank SVD/nuclear-norm; SCM growth and NNLS; conformal trajectory bands from post-treatment residuals.",
  "3. Predictive benchmarks retained as non-causal: Ridge synthetic, Bayesian ridge, Elastic Net, Huber robust, PLS latent, Random Forest, Extra Trees, Gradient Boosting, kNN synthetic, Super Learner. Flagged for overfit, not identification.",
  "4. Historical analogues kept separate as non-identified: Japan-like, Turkey-like, Italy-like late-industrialiser paths; donor year-specific p75 admissible frontier and p90 stress frontier (ex post annual envelope, country changes year to year).",
  "5. Revised NEP counterfactual as bootstrap recovery-gap process: estimate prewar log-linear trend from 1900-1913 Russian series; define annual recovery gap = potential minus observed log output per capita; estimate annual gap persistence rho from sequence of gap ratios 1921-1928; residual bootstrap uncertainty in prewar trend and persistence; for each draw log Y^NEP_t = log Y^potential_t - G1928 * rho^(t-1928) where G1928 is remaining log gap in 1928. Mechanical 1922-1928 constant-rate extrapolation retained only in stress archive, excluded from primary admissible frontier.",
  "6. Frontiers: ASCF-50 = median admissible frontier; ASCF-90 = 90th percentile of admissible frontier; Stress-90 = 90th percentile including hostile upper bounds (donor p75/p90 stress, uncapped NEP stress, population denominator stress with alternative demographic assumptions).",
  "7. Scorecard: for each Source x Treated x Endpoint compute margin = percentage difference observed cumulative growth minus frontier. Grade B = observed > ASCF-90 but < Stress-90; Grade C = observed > ASCF-50 but < ASCF-90.",
  "8. Diagnostics: pre-treatment RMSE and pre-treatment correlation for each estimator through 1940; outside conformal band indicator; pre-RMSE vs premium plot; model-family distribution.",
  "9. Donor diagnostics: largest SCM weights for GMD RUS 1940; leave-one-donor-out (27 donors each, full pool 28 implied) for each influential donor; random 75% donor subpools distribution.",
  "10. Spatial placebos: reassign treatment to donor units with same estimator; effective placebo set n=8 for verified v6 long-horizon specs; exact two-sided rank p = 1/(n_placebos+1)=0.111; post/pre RMSPE ratio.",
  "11. Forecast-origin falsification: fake treatment origins 1905->1917 horizon 12, 1913->1925 horizon 12, 1921->1928 horizon 7, 1924->1928 horizon 4, 1926->1928 horizon 2; report pseudo-effect, pre-RMSE, post-gap RMSE.",
  "12. Recovery placebos: other post-collapse rebounds (Greece, Belgium, South Africa, Venezuela) to motivate gap modelling; recovery-matched donors.",
  "13. National-account triangulation: CIA/RAND average annual GNP growth 1928-37, 1937-40, 1928-54 with two estimates A/B; end-use composition rising military share by 1940."
 ],
